 "about": "docs/proto/rain/RAIN.md; runs: docs/proto/rain/runs/<storm>_<variant>/ (20 m, LF_PARITY=1, CN x 0.91); gauge check: proto/rain/rain_gauges.py",
 "verdict": {
  "subhourly_default": false,
  "subhourly": "keep opt-in (LF_RAIN_DT=5). It works as intended: totals kept exactly, the radar timing matches ASOS 1-min gauges better than an even split, and the peak 15-min forcing rate rises 1.3-2.6x (median, Pass2 >= 5 mm/h). But on 20 m LISFLOOD-FP it moves peak depths by ~1 cm on average, catches no additional labelled site on any of the 7 storms, raises the flagged share slightly (lift down) and does not improve gauge rise or peak timing.",
  "gauge_default": false,
  "gauge": "keep opt-in (LF_RAIN_GAUGE=idw), hindcast only. Daily CoCoRaHS/COOP gauges are dense enough (12-33 per storm within the box + 0.1 deg) and show Pass2 under-catch on aug2021 (gauge/Pass2 1.32) and jul2021 (1.22); adjusting catches 3 more sites on aug2021 and 1 on jul2021 and fixes the Millbury rise, but over-shoots Northbridge, lowers lift on the 3 storms that already caught sites (aug2023, sep2023, aug2021), and the daily reports arrive the next morning, so it cannot be used live. Hourly gauges (ASOS 1-min, USGS) are too sparse (0-2 in a box) for a local hourly adjustment; they agree with Pass2 to 0.97 overall but Pass2 under-reads the >= 25 mm/h hours (0.76, n 12)."
 },
